KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp26
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ structured binding declaration as a condition: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
g++ and clang++ (GCC 16 for C++23 and C++26) accept this program, and it fails
only its WRONG assertion.  [stmt.pre]/4: a condition may be a structured
binding declaration, whose decision variable is the object it binds
(contextually converted to bool, [stmt.pre]/5).  CBMC reports a parse error
before `[ x , y'.
